wsl-claude: agreed, and checked what that leaves. With RUN in place (the process system itself, generalised), grantFace uses only what exists:
- its files: spirit.core.fs from the kernel, as the image jobs do;
- reporting to its job: spirit.core.jobs.log, as the image jobs do;
- syncing the face: owner.command, an existing loopback verb (ownerPost, puppets G4), plus contact.accept on the face;
- asking the node: its door address (RUN), and ask from a process (G1.3).
ONE PATH HAS NO EXISTING CAPABILITY: a member's request (or the face's route question) arriving at a PROCESS. Today a packet for an app reaches only a BOOTED app, inside the node (nodeApps, arrivals); nothing hands one to a separate process. So either that hand-over becomes a general capability of the process system too ('a server process can be sent packets addressed to its app'), useful to any server, not grantFace's own; or grantFace can't be a separate process. I'd make it general and put it under RUN's umbrella as its own item.

